WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.945 --> 00:00:05.350
Gara and Jonay, Two Voices on the Summit

2
00:00:06.245 --> 00:00:10.470
Gara lived in Agulo and knew every sound
of the ravines.

3
00:00:11.045 --> 00:00:17.205
One day, she looked at her reflection in
the spring and heard a warning: she must

4
00:00:17.205 --> 00:00:18.970
keep away from fire.

5
00:00:19.765 --> 00:00:22.690
Across the sea, in Tenerife, lived Jonay.

6
00:00:23.405 --> 00:00:28.170
To reach La Gomera, he used goatskin bags
to help him float.

7
00:00:28.785 --> 00:00:31.530
He swam for hours until he reached the
shore.

8
00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:37.705
When Gara and Jonay met, they walked among
the palm trees and talked until the moon

9
00:00:37.705 --> 00:00:43.145
appeared. The two of them repeated:
“Neither the sea nor the ravine can

10
00:00:43.145 --> 00:00:45.430
silence two hearts.”

11
00:00:46.165 --> 00:00:48.930
But the families feared the old warning.

12
00:00:49.665 --> 00:00:54.750
They said that Gara’s water and Jonay’s
fire must never meet.

13
00:00:55.585 --> 00:01:00.370
The young pair fled towards the summit and
asked Orahan for help.

14
00:01:01.585 --> 00:01:04.190
Their families searched for them in the
mist.

15
00:01:04.865 --> 00:01:10.425
When at last they found them, the legend
tells us that Gara and Jonay’s story came

16
00:01:10.425 --> 00:01:11.710
to a sad end.

17
00:01:12.805 --> 00:01:17.110
Their names were joined for ever in the
mountain’s name: Garajonay.

18
00:01:18.105 --> 00:01:24.025
In time, people came to understand that
hostility and failing to listen had caused

19
00:01:24.025 --> 00:01:29.825
great pain. From then on, whenever two
communities argued, someone remembered

20
00:01:29.825 --> 00:01:33.210
Gara and Jonay before closing the door to
dialogue.

21
00:01:33.965 --> 00:01:39.985
And the summit echoed back: “Neither the
sea nor the ravine can silence two

22
00:01:39.985 --> 00:01:40.985
hearts.”

